cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Critical Reconstruction Cost near Exceptional Points"
message: "If you use this code or these results, please cite this repository."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Esteves
    given-names: Maicon
    email: maicon.burn@gmail.com
date-released: 2026-08-30
abstract: >
  Universal information-cost law for parameter reconstruction near
  second-order exceptional points, validated across a 5D Einstein-Gauss-Bonnet
  black brane (nine couplings, including the acausal band), simulated and real
  superconducting qubits, a cloud QPU (ibm_fez), tabulated Kerr quasinormal
  modes, and real SXS numerical-relativity ringdowns. Includes a
  zero-fit-parameter prediction of the reconstruction rate, EP-extinction
  spectroscopy of the EGB family, and a two-task (spectral vs Petz-recovery)
  no-locking measurement.
license: MIT
version: v1.6
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.22156019
repository-code: https://github.com/maiconburn/recoverability-criticality
